Interface: inputs Enable BOOL, CurrentFloor INT, Direction INT, FullLoad BOOL, CabReq ARRAY[1..6] OF BOOL, HallReq same. Outputs HasTarget BOOL, TargetFloor INT, NextDirection INT.

Implementation: eligible(i) = CabReq[i] OR (HallReq[i] AND NOT FullLoad).

If NOT Enable or no eligible → outputs false, target=CurrentFloor, dir 0.

Else if eligible(CurrentFloor) → HasTarget TRUE, TargetFloor CurrentFloor, NextDirection 0.

Else:
 Direction=1: nearest above (min i>f with eligible); if none, nearest below (max i<f with eligible).
 Direction=-1: mirrored: nearest below (max i<f) first; if none above min i>f.
 Direction=0: nearest either side, tie to lower floor. Equivalent: choose i minimizing (abs(i-f), i). Since f not eligible. Need tie lower → compare distances; if equal choose lower.

Also NextDirection sign of TargetFloor-CurrentFloor. Could compute as comparisons, not LINT.

Need ensure all outputs set every call. Need variables local. Use INT for loop index, found flags.

Potential subtle: DT? Not needed. STruC++ supports FOR loops 1..6, arrays.

